# Binary assets must never have their line endings normalized.
#
# Git decides text vs binary by looking for a NUL byte in the first 8000
# bytes. Not every JPEG or PDF has one that early, so with core.autocrlf set
# a stray CRLF pair inside one of them would be rewritten to LF on commit and
# the file would be corrupted with no warning worth noticing. Saying so
# explicitly takes the guesswork out of it, which matters now that public/
# holds the newsletter archive.

*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
